(1986, 240, 13442, 106, 0, 0, 31, 'As the steam goes though the pipes it will lose energy to the surrounding environment. Although the pipes may be completely leak free, the effects of lost energy are the same as a leak. Insulating the steam system will require less fuel to get the necessary amount of steam to the end user. ', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-08 23:55:32'),
(1987, 239, 17306, 105, 0, 0, 11, 'Recover Flash Steam', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-18 22:44:03'),
(1988, 240, 13443, 106, 0, 0, 10, 'Exposed pipes, valves, or fittings', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-08 23:55:32'),
(1989, 239, 17307, 105, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Typically a percentage of condensate flashes back to steam when it enters an atmospheric condensate line from a high pressure steam line. A low pressure condensate line can be used to retain this flash steam. It can be combined with cold incoming makeup water in a flash tank capturing the \"distilled water\" of the flash steam and increasing the final makeup water temperature. Often there is more energy available in the flash steam than can be used with the makeup water. It can also be used in other low temperature processes that can use the moisture and heat.</p>', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-18 22:44:03'),
