(2288, 257, 18344, 272, 0, 0, 11, 'Recover heat rejected from condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2289, 257, 18345, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Often, heat rejected from the condensers can be used to heat a nearby process stream, lowering the associated heating load.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2290, 257, 18346, 272, 0, 1, 10, 'A low-temperature process is located nearby water-cooled condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2291, 257, 18347, 272, 0, 2, 12, '<p>Install split condensers to reduce the cooling tower load. A split condenser first uses a nearby process stream to precool the refrigerant before it enters a second condenser that uses cooling tower water.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2292, 257, 18348, 272, 0, 1, 3, '14,500 Btu/hr per ton produced is rejected in the condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2293, 257, 18349, 272, 0, 0, 15, '<p>Data to collect</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2294, 257, 18350, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Refrigeration capacity (tons)', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2295, 257, 18351, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Temperature of refrigerant entering the condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2296, 257, 18352, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Temperature of the process stream to be heated', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2297, 257, 18353, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Mass flow rates of refrigerant and process stream', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2298, 257, 18354, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Refrigerant and process fluid properties', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2299, 257, 18355, 272, 0, 0, 11, 'Insulate hot/cold surfaces', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2300, 257, 18356, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Un-insulated cold/hot lines or tanks create unnecessary heat transfer and can result in large energy losses. Simply adding appropriate insulation on these surfaces will result in substantial energy savings.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2301, 257, 18357, 272, 0, 1, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-130', 'See Insulation on the Thermal Systems page for more information', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2302, 257, 18358, 272, 0, 0, 11, 'Use hot gas defrost', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2303, 257, 18359, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p><em class=\"ql-size-small\">Lets talk about this one.- Joe</em></p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2304, 257, 18360, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p>When air cooling units operate below 32 ºF, frost inevitably builds up on evaporator coils. Frost acts as an insulator and hinders heat exchanger performance. As a result, a defrost cycle must be implemented for these systems.</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2305, 257, 18361, 272, 0, 1, 12, 'Cycle hot refrigerant from the compressor discharge through the evaporator coils to melt frost.', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2306, 257, 18362, 272, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Heats coils from the inside so less heat is transferred to the surrounding air</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2307, 257, 18363, 272, 0, 1, 2, '<p>More complex system design and higher implementation cost</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2308, 257, 18364, 272, 0, 1, 3, 'Savings will generally be on the order of 10-20% of the total system use', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2309, 257, 18365, 272, 0, 1, 4, '<p>Suitable only for larger systems with multiple evaporators. In order to use hot gas, the system needs to produce it. While one evaporator is defrosting the others will run; at least two to three evaporators running for each evaporator defrosting is required for low-moderate temperature systems.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2310, 257, 18366, 272, 0, 0, 15, '<p>Data to collect</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2311, 257, 18367, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Defrost cycle schedule ', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2312, 257, 18368, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Power of the current electric defrost system', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2313, 257, 18369, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Distance from compressor discharge to evaporators to determine the amount of piping required', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-03-21 19:10:04'),
(2314, 258, 18472, 9, 0, 0, 1, 'Versatile. Offers compact energy density. ', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 15:57:47'),
(2315, 258, 18473, 9, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Spark free for potentially explosive environments.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 15:57:47'),
(2316, 258, 18474, 9, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Can be used as an easy quick fix for many issues.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 15:57:47'),
(2317, 258, 18475, 9, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Familiar utility for industrial personnel.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 15:57:47'),
(2318, 258, 18476, 9, 0, 0, 1, 'A single mechanical energy input at the compressor can be distributed throughout a facility. ', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 15:57:47'),
(2319, 259, 18477, 16, 0, 0, 4, '<p>Take care to avoid potential dangerous air injection associated with directing compressed air flow directly onto skin.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 15:58:04'),
(2320, 260, 20402, 17, 0, 0, 7, 'Looped distribution systems can help maintain uniform pressure throughout a compressed air system.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-13 18:37:13'),
(2321, 260, 20403, 17, 0, 0, 7, '<p>Well sized compressed air lines reduce pressure loss.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-13 18:37:13'),
(2322, 260, 20404, 17, 0, 0, 7, '<p>A well designed compressed air system should typically have a maximum 10 psi pressure drop in delivering air to any end-use in the system.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-13 18:37:13'),
(2323, 261, 18478, 18, 0, 0, 3, '<p>Expect a 1% drop in compressor energy and cost per 2 PSI in compressor outlet pressure drop.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 16:00:01'),
(2324, 261, 18479, 18, 0, 0, 3, '<p>85 psi is the standard required minimum inlet pressure for most common industrial pneumatic equipment.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 16:00:01'),
(2325, 261, 18480, 18, 0, 0, 3, '<p>80% to 90% of energy for compressed air is lost as heat.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 16:00:01'),
(2326, 261, 18481, 18, 0, 0, 3, '<p>Over 5 HP of electrical power is required for each 1 HP of compressed air power.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 16:00:01'),
(2327, 262, 18485, 19, 0, 0, 8, '<p>Use a pressure gage with standard quick connects typically used in compressed air lines to diagnose line pressure drops.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 16:01:01'),
(2328, 262, 18486, 19, 0, 0, 8, '<p>Determine the leak load by checking compressor output when there is no productive air use.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-29 16:01:01'),
