(15956, 109, 0, 0, 8, '<p><strong>Slip Measurement</strong> - For AC induction/asynchronous motors, \"slip\" offers one way to estimate motor load if amps or power are not obtainable. For example, if a nominal 1800 RPM motor nameplate lists an RPM of 1750 (for full-load), the actual reduction in RPM with load is linear with the percent of full load. For example, if you use a strobe to measure an RPM of 1775 RPM on the same motor, then the motor load factor is 50%. If it is a 100 HP motor, it is working against a 50 HP load.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-22 20:56:20', 1, '', ''),
(15957, 110, 0, 0, 7, '<p>Serve high operating hour, high horsepower loads with premium efficiency motors.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-22 20:59:22', 1, '', ''),
(15958, 110, 0, 0, 7, '<p>For optimum belt drive efficiency, set and maintain correct tensioning and alignment on belt drives.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-22 20:59:22', 1, '', ''),
