(16418, 224, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Generally, different classes of rate schedules are assigned to consumers based on the application and type of electricity demanded.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 22:40:16', 0, '', ''),
(16419, 224, 0, 0, 26, 'An industrial, three-phase rate schedule is commonly assigned to industry consumers.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 22:40:16', 0, '', ''),
(16420, 224, 0, 0, 26, '<p>The specific details and charges of a rate schedule varies depending on the electric company.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 22:40:16', 0, '', ''),
(16421, 224, 0, 0, 12, 'Consult the rate schedule provided by your electric company for your rates and charges.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 22:40:16', 0, '', ''),
(16588, 230, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Base charge: </strong>This charge does not vary with use. It is a basic monthly meter charge to have natural gas available</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:01:00', 0, '', ''),
(16589, 230, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Commodity charge: </strong>the cost of gas used</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:01:00', 0, '', ''),
(16590, 230, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Transport fees: </strong>the cost to transport gas from its source to the industry site.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:01:00', 0, '', ''),
(16591, 230, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Taxes</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:01:00', 0, '', ''),
(16592, 230, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Public purpose charge: </strong>These may indicate availability of utility incentives for energy efficiency projects.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:01:00', 0, '', ''),
(16660, 229, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Natural gas charges based on use may be divided into two, distinct categories</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 17, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16661, 229, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Commodity Charge</strong>: the cost of the gas itself</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16662, 229, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Transmission/Distribution Charge</strong>: the cost to transport gas from its source to the industry site.</p><p></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16663, 229, 0, 0, 31, '<p>This reflects two methods of obtaining gas:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16664, 229, 0, 0, 31, '<p>1. Gas purchased from and directly transported by the local gas company. (Commodity and transmission charges are both determined by local gas company.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16665, 229, 0, 0, 31, '<p>2. Gas is purchased from a third party vendor and transported by the local gas company. (Commodity charges are determined by a third party; transmission charges come from the local gas company) Gas purchased from a third party on the open market can be cheaper than gas purchased from the local utility. Prices typically vary month to month.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16666, 229, 0, 0, 31, '<p></p><p><strong>Interruptible Rates</strong>: Utilities may offer interruptible rate schedules. The unit cost for gas can be reduced if the site agrees that their supply can be interrupted on rare occasion when regional use exceeds supply.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16667, 229, 0, 0, 31, '<p></p><p>The specific details and charges of a rate schedule vary depending on the gas company and any third party, if applicable.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16668, 229, 0, 0, 12, '<p>Consult the rate schedule provided by your gas company and third party vendor for your rates and charges.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:10:05', 0, '', ''),
(16743, 232, 0, 0, 31, 'Generally, water companies assign different classes of rate schedules depending on the application.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:25:21', 0, '', ''),
(16744, 232, 0, 1, 26, 'An industrial or commercial rate schedule is often assigned to industry consumers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:25:21', 0, '', ''),
(16745, 232, 0, 0, 31, 'The specific details and charges of a rate schedule often varies depending on the water company.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:25:21', 0, '', ''),
(16746, 232, 0, 1, 12, 'Consult the rate schedule provided by your electric company for your rates and charges.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-02-24 23:25:21', 0, '', ''),
(16807, 284, 0, 0, 17, '<p></p>', '/uploads/user_55/f0ea8b8362ecc6ca6a487bf1f1d96e5a.pdf', 'Pump Data Collection Sheet', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-09 00:10:32', 0, '', ''),
(16808, 182, 0, 0, 4, '<p>When modifying or replacing pumps and fans, system pressure or head should not exceed the maximum pressure or head the fan or pump can sustain. Surge points should be avoided. (Surge points occur when a fan or pump can operate at two different flows at the same pressure).</p>', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 17:42:59', 0, '', ''),
(16809, 182, 0, 0, 4, 'Improperly designed pump systems can lead to low pressures at the pump inlet which can lead to cavitation. This can seriously damage the pump and reduce its operating life.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 17:42:59', 0, '', ''),
(16810, 182, 0, 0, 24, 'Online resource discussing how cavitation occurs and how to detect and prevent it from happening.', 'https://modernpumpingtoday.com/detecting-pump-cavitation/', 'Detecting Pump Cavitation', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-09 22:43:02', 0, '', ''),
(16843, 223, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Electrical utilities can measure and charge for electrical use based on:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 15, '2021-03-07 20:24:22', 0, '', ''),
(16844, 223, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Energy Used</strong>: measured in units of kilowatt-hours (kWh).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:24:22', 0, '', ''),
(16845, 223, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Demand</strong>: (or the greatest rate of energy use) measured in units of kilowatts (kW). (Often the greatest average 5 minute kW demand during peak demand hours in a month).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:24:22', 0, '', ''),
(16846, 223, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Reactive Power</strong>: measured in different ways depending on the provider and it may be a significant contributor to energy costs (see Power Factor Correction page for more information)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:24:22', 0, '', ''),
(16847, 223, 0, 1, 28, '<p></p>', 'https://walkthrough.eec.oregonstate.edu/wiki/utilities/61', 'Power Factor Correction', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:24:22', 0, '', ''),
(16848, 223, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Electric companies may charge different rates per kWh or kW depending on the time of day. For example, rates during nighttime hours can be less than daytime. The higher rate is referred to as \"on-peak\" while the lower rate is considered \"off-peak\". This idea can also apply to seasonal rates that change depending on the time of year.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 16, '2021-03-07 20:24:22', 0, '', ''),
(16849, 223, 0, 0, 12, '<p>  Consult your provider\'s rate schedule to find these rates, if applicable.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:24:22', 0, '', ''),
(16850, 294, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Analyzing utilities is an excellent way to quantify total energy use, identify where energy is used, and reveal trends that are not readily apparent from individual billing statements alone. Additionally, a utility analysis estimate also can indicate the areas where implementing more efficient technologies or practices will yield the greatest savings.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:24:56', 0, '', ''),
(16930, 228, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Natural gas is most often measured in units of heat: Therms or British Thermal Units (Btu). </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:14', 0, '', ''),
(16931, 228, 0, 0, 3, '<p>There are 10 Therms in a Btu</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:14', 0, '', ''),
(16932, 225, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Base Charge</strong>: This charge does not vary with use. It is a basic monthly meter charge to have electricity available.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:59', 0, '', ''),
(16933, 225, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Metered Energy Use Charge</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:59', 0, '', ''),
(16934, 225, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Metered Demand Charge</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:59', 0, '', ''),
(16935, 225, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Metered Reactive Power Charge</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:59', 0, '', ''),
(16936, 225, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Taxes</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:59', 0, '', ''),
(16937, 225, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Public Purpose Charges: </strong>These may indicate availability of utility incentives for energy efficiency projects.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 20:45:59', 0, '', ''),
(16938, 231, 0, 0, 31, '<p><strong>Demanded Water</strong> (Fresh water consumed): Typically measured in volumetric units of hundred cubic feet (HCF) or liters (L).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16939, 231, 0, 0, 31, '<p><strong>Effluent Water</strong> (Wastewater discharged): Often deemed to be the same volume as fresh water demanded.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16940, 231, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Effluent characteristics are often charged to incentivize a higher degree of water treatment.  This minimizes the cost to treat the water at the wastewater plant as well as any potentially adverse effects when the effluent is reintroduced to the surrounding environment.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16941, 231, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>Biological Oxygen Demand (BOD): </strong>This is the amount of dissolved oxygen aerobic microorganisms use to decompose organic matter in the water. It is measured in units of milligrams per liter (mg/L).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16942, 231, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>Chemical Oxygen Demand (COD): </strong>This quantifies the amount of oxygen that would be required to oxidize organic chemicals in the water.  It is measured in units of milligrams per liter (mg/L).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16943, 231, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>Total Suspended Solids (TSS):</strong> This is the dry weight of suspended particulates in water. It is measured in units of milligrams per liter (mg/L).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16944, 231, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>pH: </strong>This is a measure of how basic or acidic the water is.  It is measured from 0-14 on a non-dimensional scale.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16945, 231, 0, 1, 31, 'Some water companies may use generalized, volumetric measurements for effluent water instead of BOD and TSS.  Additionally, some companies may add a charge for stormwater volumes as well.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16946, 231, 0, 0, 12, 'Examine the rate schedule provided by your water company to determine how your effluent is being charged.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-07 21:00:23', 0, '', ''),
(16953, 265, 0, 0, 17, 'Thermodynamic properties of water/steam from the Heat Exchanger Design Handbook by C. F. Beaton, published in 1986. This is useful for finding the enthalpy of water/steam for calculating heat transfer.', 'http://thermopedia.com/content/1150/', 'Water/Steam Property Tables', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-01 22:28:21', 1, '', ''),
