(17188, 125, 0, 0, 32, '', '/uploads/user_55/215ed3c31cbc4dec9d0ffcdc21ee5a39.jpg', 'Sample Pump Curve', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-09 22:42:43', 0, '', ''),
(17189, 125, 0, 0, 32, '', '/uploads/user_55/83a92c72662cbec1f08d0c7686c6af33.jpg', 'Sample Pump Nameplate', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-09 22:42:43', 0, '', ''),
(17190, 125, 0, 0, 8, '<p>Keep in mind that flow and head information on a pump nameplate only reflect design conditions, actual flow and head can be different if the connected pumping network has changed from its original design characteristics.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-09 22:42:43', 0, '', ''),
(17191, 276, 0, 0, 14, 'Why is the incremental cost of a meter relatively low?', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17192, 276, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Some providers allow customers to purchase a utility using the wholesale market price, or just the raw cost of the utility, rather than charging additional operational fees.  This tends to reduce the total amount charged and thus can be a contributor to low incremental meter costs.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17193, 276, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Additionally, some providers may sell at the wholesale market price up to a certain threshold before adding the operational fees.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17194, 276, 0, 1, 12, '<p>Consult your provider\'s website or utility representative for more information.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17195, 276, 0, 0, 14, 'What is reactive power and how is it charged?', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17196, 276, 0, 1, 28, '<p></p>', 'https://walkthrough.eec.oregonstate.edu/wiki/utilities/61', 'Power Factor Correction', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17197, 276, 0, 0, 14, 'What if there are numerous meters under $500 per month?', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17198, 276, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Some small meters may be consolidated into one for analysis purposes.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17199, 276, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Alternatively, other small meters significantly less than $500 per month may be omitted from analysis.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17200, 276, 0, 0, 14, 'Why does the published rate schedules from the provider not match the rates on the bills?', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17201, 276, 0, 1, 26, 'Check the publish date on the rate schedule.  It may be outdated, particularly for online resources.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17202, 276, 0, 1, 12, '<p>Use the most recent rate for analysis, even if it is found on the billing statements and not the rate schedule.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
(17203, 276, 0, 1, 8, '<p>These analyses are estimates. It is okay if discrepancies between the bills and the rate schedules exist.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-03-10 22:35:45', 0, '', ''),
