(19393, 307, 0, 0, 31, '<p>CHP is one of the primary tools used to increase the resilience of current infrastructure. Resiliency planning refers to systems that are designed to continue operations during disturbances in the utility grid. Commonly technology is dependent on electricity and natural gas which are vulnerable to the stability of the grid. For critical operations, such as hospitals, even momentary outages can result in disasters. CHP systems are often implemented as an alternative or backup to the grid. They have the ability to provide instant power, and can be started even durring a complete blackout. Well designed CHP systems can sustain normal operations independently for multiday outages. There are several cases where infrastructure with CHP systems provided shelter during natural disasters, such as hurricanes.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-10 21:43:22', 0, '', ''),
(19394, 307, 0, 0, 24, '<p>Briefly outlines how CHP is a critical part of infrastructure resiliency</p>', 'https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2020/07/f76/CHP_Resilience_Policy_Planning_May2020.pdf', 'DOE CHP Resiliency Planning', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-10 21:43:22', 0, '', 'sha384-7CAt5vYQLsoAD1vLiX0ctvSQA4xvpfVj2p7j3p0dc3tHGXgwROCFYVJbQ7lmcyEQ'),
