(19648, 99, 0, 0, 17, '<p>DOE page that highlights the benefits of steam.</p>', 'https://oregonstate.app.box.com/file/508954521092?s=wwbza574dop3pazrfz24252h6qzdgkbf', 'Tools to Boost Steam System Efficiency', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:04', 1, '', ''),
(19649, 103, 0, 0, 31, '<p>As water is evaporated to steam, solids in the water remain in the solution. To keep dissolved solids from building up to excessive levels, the boiler water is drained and replaced with fresh water. This is called \"blow-down\". The difference in temperature between the replacement water and the hot boiler water represents an energy loss. To minimize this loss, blow-down should be keep to the minimum required to keep dissolved solids at an acceptable level. The rate of continuous blow-down depends on the quality of the feedwater and the amount of condensate returned.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:47', 0, '', ''),
(19650, 103, 0, 0, 1, 'Reducing blow-down will also reduce the amount of water treatment chemicals required', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:47', 0, '', ''),
(19651, 103, 0, 0, 11, 'Minimize the continuous blowdown rate with a conductivity sensor', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:47', 0, '', ''),
(19652, 103, 0, 0, 11, 'Install blowdown heat recovery', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:47', 0, '', ''),
(19653, 103, 0, 1, 21, '<p>An OSU EEC Analysis Template in Microsoft Excel Format (old style)</p>', 'https://oregonstate.box.com/s/vnmiftvhluyq9pdhdl5g28w4wswdue1m', 'Install Blowdown Heat Recovery Templet', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:47', 0, '', ''),
(19654, 104, 0, 0, 11, 'Replace damper controls on draft fans with variable speed control', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:53', 0, '', ''),
(19655, 104, 0, 1, 21, '<p>An OSU EEC Analysis Template in Microsoft Excel Format (old style)</p>', 'https://oregonstate.box.com/s/n624ppslvyk702vo3931oioyyxq755fd', 'Install Boiler Fan VFD Templet', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:05:53', 0, '', ''),
(19656, 105, 0, 0, 15, 'Condensate flow and temperature', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19657, 105, 0, 0, 11, 'Return more/all condensate back to the boiler', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19658, 105, 0, 1, 21, '<p>An OSU EEC Analysis Template in Microsoft Excel Format (unapproved)</p>', 'https://oregonstate.box.com/s/t93pfp1kwqvbw7wjporoo1i6yv1f1ril', 'Recover Condensate Templet', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19659, 105, 0, 0, 11, 'Recover Flash Steam', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19660, 105, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Typically a percentage of condensate flashes back to steam when it enters an atmospheric condensate line from a high pressure steam line. A low pressure condensate line can be used to retain and direct this flash steam. It can be combined with cold incoming makeup water in a flash tank capturing the \"distilled water\" of the flash steam and increasing the final makeup water temperature. Often there is more energy available in the flash steam than can be used with the makeup water. It can also be used in other low temperature processes that can use the moisture and heat. (An example might be low pressure steam used for block conditioning of log sections before peeling into a veneer.)</p>', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19661, 105, 0, 1, 10, 'Steam being released into atmosphere from the boiler system', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19662, 105, 0, 1, 1, 'Payback period is usually within a year', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19663, 105, 0, 1, 1, 'Capturing and reusing the steam can reduce hog fuel by 14.5%', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19664, 105, 0, 1, 1, 'Condensate does not require any chemical treatment other than condensate polishing. ', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19665, 105, 0, 1, 31, 'A condensate polisher is similar to a water softener. Polishing removes the trace amount of mineral that are dissolved in the condensate after running though the boiler. ', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19666, 105, 0, 1, 2, 'Maintenance crews will need training to work with steam recovery systems', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19667, 105, 0, 1, 2, 'There are usually no incentives for this opportunity, because the system usually pays for itself within a year.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19668, 105, 0, 1, 3, 'A good recovery system can collect up to 80% of the condensate', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19669, 105, 0, 1, 3, 'Steam recovery is most efficient when waste heat is high and flow is continuous', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19670, 105, 0, 1, 8, 'Multiple different types of steam traps available to fit company needs: Mechanical, Thermodynamic, or Thermostatic', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
(19671, 105, 0, 1, 17, 'Contains specific information about flash steam recovery', 'https://www.energy.gov/sites/prod/files/2014/05/f16/steam12_lowpressure_steam.pdf', 'DOE Tip Sheet Flash Steam Recovery', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', 'sha384-jD3QcNeDY/uVNOe2UN6icM4RNWzS1i98YvRLWJYxUarqKlmPERcCJmX1fgFL9Gws'),
(19672, 105, 0, 1, 21, '<p></p>', 'https://oregonstate.box.com/s/9sgjyfdldo1tdi6c5jitu08zm8vho77r', 'Flash Steam Recovery', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-11 18:06:09', 0, '', ''),
