(20402, 17, 0, 0, 7, 'Looped distribution systems can help maintain uniform pressure throughout a compressed air system.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-13 18:37:13', 1, '', ''),
(20403, 17, 0, 0, 7, '<p>Well sized compressed air lines reduce pressure loss.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-13 18:37:13', 1, '', ''),
(20404, 17, 0, 0, 7, '<p>A well designed compressed air system should typically have a maximum 10 psi pressure drop in delivering air to any end-use in the system.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-13 18:37:13', 1, '', ''),
(20405, 233, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Base Charge</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20406, 233, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Demanded Water</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20407, 233, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Effluent Water</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20408, 233, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>BOD Waste</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20409, 233, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>TSS Waste</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20410, 233, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>Stormwater Rate</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20411, 233, 0, 1, 26, '<p><strong>Sewer Rate</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20412, 233, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Tax</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20413, 233, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Public Purpose Charge</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20414, 233, 0, 0, 26, '<p>(Have you ever seen Public Purpose Charges on water?) There\'s instructions about it in our UA template, but I haven\'t done enough of them to know. [I made it internal so it won\'t be forgotten, but not published until its seen consistently. -Ali]</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:41:26', 0, '', ''),
(20415, 295, 0, 0, 31, '<p>1. Gather at least 12-14 consecutive months of billing statements.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20416, 295, 0, 1, 31, '<p>For this at the EEC, either the clients directly provide us with their bills or they send back a utility release form in the pre-assessment package (PAP). For the latter, baseline takes the release form and directly obtains the bills from the provider using the Utility Contacts and Companies spreadsheet.</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20417, 295, 0, 0, 31, '<p>2. Table the breakdowns of the monthly charges for each meter individually</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20418, 295, 0, 1, 8, 'Spreadsheet applications and software such as Microsoft Excel are helpful tools.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20419, 295, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Each meter gets one table that breaks down the monthly utility charges for the year under examination.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20420, 295, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Ex. For an electricity meter, log the energy used (in kWh), the demand (in kW-mo), and the reactive power (in kVAR).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20421, 295, 0, 0, 31, '<p>3. Identify the rate charge for the utility either from the provider or the billing statements.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20422, 295, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Also identify any additional charges that are applicable such as a tax or other utility specific rates.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20423, 295, 0, 2, 31, '<p>Ex. For an electricity meter, the reactive power rate charge should be identified for accurate accounting.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20424, 295, 0, 0, 31, '<p>4. Calculate the monetary costs and any other pertinent information of each breakdown using the meter tables and rate schedules.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20425, 295, 0, 1, 31, 'Ex. For electricity, calculating the Power Factor from the reactive power given in statements is useful for examining whether implementing power factor correction solutions will result in annual cost savings.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20426, 295, 0, 1, 31, 'Calculating quantity and cost averages per month is very useful for examining trends and areas of opportunity for annual savings.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20427, 295, 0, 1, 8, 'Pay close attention to the billing statements and the rate schedules if differing charge rates apply to the utility (ex. on and off-peak demand for electricity).', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20428, 295, 0, 0, 31, '<p>5. Graph or chart parameters of interest to examine trends.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20429, 295, 0, 1, 31, 'Ex. For electricity, graphing the month against the energy used provides a visual on when equipment on that meter use the most energy during the year, and charting the percentage of energy use, demand, and other fees for the meter can visually show where the greatest potential for savings lie.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20430, 295, 0, 0, 21, '<p>This document outlines the basic steps the OSU EEC follows in performing a utility analysis.</p>', '/uploads/user_54/4e9d712372e833aed306db8a1b090257.pdf', 'Utility Analysis Checklist', 3, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 18:14:36', 0, '', ''),
(20431, 295, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Made internal until formatting is reviewed. -Ali</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
(20432, 295, 0, 0, 21, '<p>This is the EEC template for utility analyses.  It is set up with center headers and prepared cells for our use for IAC reports</p>', 'https://oregonstate.box.com/s/nafls9za4zx6ht4sj4kfyyx5kklqvz95', 'UA Template', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 18:14:46', 0, '', ''),
(20433, 295, 0, 0, 17, '<p>This spreadsheet logs utility contacts and companies for bill collection.</p>', 'https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/17epS8LjMsdfI0EDfMiSsot0_94LERR6jfo0U2mSPMPg/edit?gid=1815063488&pli=1#gid=1204136668', 'Utility Contacts/Companies Spreadsheet', 1, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-14 16:47:46', 0, '', ''),
