(20682, 318, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Is the stack temperature too high?</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-27 19:06:58', 0, '', ''),
(20683, 318, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Is the furnace, oven or direct fire operating at incomplete combustion?</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-27 19:06:58', 0, '', ''),
(20684, 318, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Are there any opportunities for heat recovery?</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-27 19:06:58', 0, '', ''),
(20685, 318, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Is the efficiency and performance of the system being monitored manually?</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-27 19:06:58', 0, '', ''),
(20733, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Ballast</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20734, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>A device that limits the amount of current running through certain bulbs.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20735, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Ballast Factor</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20736, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Measure of actual lumen output compared to the rated lumen output.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20737, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>The amount of light that reaches a certain area.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20738, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Fixture</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20739, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>A device that holds certain amounts of lamps and allows for its replacement.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20740, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Lamp</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20741, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>A device that holds certain amounts of lamps and allows for its replacement.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20742, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Lighting Efficacy</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20743, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Represented by Lumens/Watt, is a measure of how well a bulb emits light over the amount of power required. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20744, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Lumens<span>﻿</span></strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20745, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>The amount of light a bulb emits.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20746, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Lumen Depreciation</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20747, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Reflects the overall performance of a lamp over its life, certain bulbs have certain rated depreciation values.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20748, 319, 0, 0, 26, '<p><strong>Restrike Time</strong></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20749, 319, 0, 1, 31, '<p>The time it takes an arc tube (in high-intensity discharge bulbs) to cool down enough to be turned back on.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-28 17:39:52', 0, '', ''),
(20758, 247, 0, 0, 31, '<p>At its core, simulation is a way to \"What if...?\" A good simulation will simplify a physical system in a way that produces the same results without requiring the actual system to change. In industry simulations are useful for modeling how a machine will function to predict failures, finding bottlenecks in processes, identifying potential cash flow issues and training employees.</p>', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:03:08', 0, '', ''),
(20759, 247, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Small scale simulation is an often overlooked part of manufacturing. Although think of the CAD models that contain moving parts, there are many opportunities for simulations of financial outcomes that would be to complex to solve with deterministic or stochastic models. One of the common tools for such a situations call Crystal Ball. Financial simulation are most practical when they are designed by an seasoned decision maker who can use their intuition and knowledge about the process to make sure the simulation is accurate, opposed to a computer programmer who lacks the knowledge about the real world system.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:03:08', 0, '', ''),
(20760, 249, 0, 0, 31, '<p>The roots for cloud computing come from early days of computers where a centralized computer would serve several terminals. Nowadays cloud computing is a way for low power computers (such as tablets and smart phones) to utilize the Internet to send information to a centralized computing system that contains software and hardware that are designed for complex calculation. </p>', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:08:05', 0, '', ''),
(20771, 309, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Conventional subtractive manufacturing is with a series of processes that remove material. Individually processes are usually time efficient, but as a system there is a lot of waiting, setup and inspection. Additionally the parts that can be created are often limited by the size and geometry of the cutting tool. By using a single machine to incremental build up a part, a single additive manufacturing machine can do the same work as multiple conventional processes. This commonly reduces the wait time between machines, and the setup and inspection when moving to the next process. It is also is able to build complex parts that could not be built with conventional methods. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20772, 309, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Because of the speed at which small parts can be produced, industry often refers to \"rapid prototyping\". Since production lines are so specialized to mass produce a single part, the cost associated with training the operators and retooling the machines means high costs for event the simplest prototypes. Once the CAD models are done, minimal modification are needed to being prototyping with additive methods.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20773, 309, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Since the process is completely computer controlled, it can run without operator supervision and often can be left running over night.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20774, 309, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Can produce complex geometry that conventional methods cannot</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20775, 309, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Process is highly flexible. Switching between parts no longer requires machine changeover, retooling, or retraining operators</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20776, 309, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Can produce functionally graded alloys that otherwise would not be cost effective</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20777, 309, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Can reduce weight by making porous structures inside a \"solid\" part </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20778, 309, 0, 0, 2, '<p>Process has limited ability to be optimized for speed. Not meant to be used in an assembly line or flow shop</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20779, 309, 0, 0, 2, '<p>May have low tolerances. Often speed is traded for precision requiring expensive post processing (machining)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20780, 309, 0, 0, 2, '<p>Specialty powders and wires are costly</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:37:09', 0, '', ''),
(20781, 253, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Machine Learning refers to algorithms that allow a machine to update its program to better match the desired output. At its core machine learning is linear algebra and statistics, which makes it very similar to mathematic regression models. The advantage is that these algorithms do not assume that the process follows any particular model (i.e. linearity, interaction between variables, significance of variables, or independence of variables)</p>', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:44:39', 0, '', ''),
(20782, 253, 0, 0, 31, '<p>For small companies where they vary multiple process parameters to get different outcomes, a machine learning system can be developed to help find the ideal parameters for each outcome. </p>', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:44:39', 0, '', ''),
(20783, 321, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Optimize process though simulation</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:55:04', 0, '', ''),
(20784, 321, 0, 1, 26, '<p>By running many different combinations of variables you can quantitively see what combination produces the best results</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:55:04', 0, '', ''),
(20785, 321, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Optimize process though machine learning models </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:55:04', 0, '', ''),
(20786, 321, 0, 1, 26, '<p>By feeding a computer historical data about a process, the machine can learn and start to interpolate variables to figure out the best combinations for a given process. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:55:04', 0, '', ''),
(20787, 321, 0, 0, 8, '<p>If the company has the capability, a machine learning algorithm can feed data to a simulation to run virtually tests and \"learn\" new information without requiring any physical tests done. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 00:55:04', 0, '', ''),
(20795, 322, 0, 0, 31, '<p>The development of robotics that could be programed to perform a single repetitive task is generally considered the start of the third industrial revolution. Since that time robots have become significantly more complex and interconnected. Today robots utilize software coupled with an array of sensors that allow them to have \"intelligent behavior\". Robots that work directly with humans, or \"Cobots\", are designed to react and adapt to human behavior (much study has be done to try to make an operator teach a cobot what to do without need to write lines of code). </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 01:18:05', 0, '', ''),
(20796, 322, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Highly adaptable</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 01:18:05', 0, '', ''),
(20797, 322, 0, 0, 2, '<p>Expensive, price is rapidly reducing</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 01:18:05', 0, '', ''),
(20813, 323, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Drones for survey</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20814, 323, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Need a description that encompasses all the capabilities, such as survey land and facilities. Need this to not sound like drones preparing to strike or used as an alternative to security camera</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20815, 323, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Moves faster can people</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20816, 323, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Can get birds eye view of facility</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20817, 323, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Does not require people to go to unsafe places</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20818, 323, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Drones for delivery</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20819, 323, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Although this is mostly an idea in my head, the amount of time saved by using drones to deliver small packages could be huge.</p><p>Imagine setting up landing sites such as mail boxes. Your boss in building 3 asks you to deliver a package to building 47. Instead of spending the time to trek that package across the campus, you send airmail via drone. </p><p>For more on this see the article by Goodchild and Toy.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20820, 323, 0, 2, 17, '<p>Link to ScienceDirect article describing feasibility of drone delivery as an alternative to delivery trucks.</p>', 'http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S136192091630133X', 'Delivery by Drone: Evaluation of CO2 emissions', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:33:58', 0, '', ''),
(20821, 250, 0, 0, 17, 'Springer', 'http://link.springer.com/10.1007/s10586-017-0767-x', 'Yang et al.  “Towards product customization and personalization in IoT-enabled cloud manufacturing,”', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:35:33', 0, '', ''),
(20822, 250, 0, 0, 24, 'Science Direct', 'http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0925527314002825', 'Guo et al. “An RFID-based intelligent decision support system architecture for production monitoring and scheduling in a distributed manufacturing environment,”', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:35:33', 0, '', ''),
(20823, 250, 0, 0, 24, 'MDPI (Open Source)', 'https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/6/1/14', 'T. Kamigaki, “Object‐Oriented RFID with IoT: A Design Concept of Information Systems in Manufacturing,”', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-04-30 05:35:33', 0, '', ''),
