(20878, 324, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Compressor Data</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:36:34', 1, '', ''),
(20879, 324, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Type (Rotary Screw, Centrifugal, Reciprocating)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:36:34', 1, '', ''),
(20880, 324, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Nameplate data </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:36:34', 1, '', ''),
(20881, 324, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Operation hours</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:36:34', 1, '', ''),
(20882, 324, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Live power readings</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:36:34', 1, '', ''),
(20883, 324, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Power over time (data loggers set up for at least one week)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:36:34', 1, '', ''),
(20884, 8, 0, 0, 8, 'Reduced air pressure not only reduces air compressor energy required for a set volume of air, it will also result in less air volume consumed by leaks and unregulated air uses (although it can be hard to estimate the volume reduction).\r\n', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20885, 8, 0, 0, 3, '<p>Expect a 1% drop in compressor energy and cost per 2 PSI in compressor outlet pressure drop (for standard nominal ~100 PSI range systems).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20886, 8, 0, 0, 11, 'Reduce compressed air system pressure to the 95-100 PSI range.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20887, 8, 0, 1, 10, 'System pressure is set over 100 PSI for a compressed air system serving standard industrial utilities and controls.\r\n', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20888, 8, 0, 1, 8, '<p>Check end use requirements. Most equipment requires ~ 85 PSI. Allowing for a 10 PSI system distribution pressure drop should allow the minimum pressure to be set for 95 PSI.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20889, 8, 0, 1, 8, '<p>Incrementally drop pressure while checking to ensure no production issues occur.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20890, 8, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data to Collect:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20891, 8, 0, 2, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-06-07 16:56:52', 0, '', ''),
(20892, 8, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Collect pressure settings: current and proposed.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20893, 8, 0, 1, 17, 'An OSU EEC Analysis Template in Microsoft Excel Format', 'https://drive.google.com/open?id=1ZrFL3Cc2rmiRL-lkODnqn4smkZo7BiRX', 'Analysis Template: Reduce Compressed Air Pressure ', 2, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-27 22:10:13', 0, '', ''),
(20894, 8, 0, 1, 12, 'Reduce line pressure losses in compressed air distribution system:', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20895, 8, 0, 2, 10, 'Pressure drops more than 10 PSI from the compressor to any location at any time (particularly remote locations or near shorter duration high volume uses)?', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20896, 8, 0, 2, 8, '<p>Pay close attention to oil filters, complex fittings, poor takeoffs, and bottlenecked and overly small pipe diameters.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20897, 8, 0, 2, 8, '<p>Critically evaluate regulator placement and settings.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20898, 8, 0, 1, 12, 'Add receivers close to equipment with periodic high volume air uses (that might be creating local pressure drops).', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20899, 8, 0, 2, 10, 'Local pressure drops periodically appear in parts of the system .', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20900, 8, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Serve high pressure compressed air end use with a separate system or a booster.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20901, 8, 0, 1, 10, 'An entire plant air system is set at a high pressure because a few pieces of equipment require higher pressure air.		', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20902, 8, 0, 1, 15, 'Inventory equipment needing higher than average pressures, noting minimum pressure and estimating air volume required.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:39:24', 0, '', ''),
(20941, 27, 0, 0, 31, 'Energy savings associated with reductions in compressed air use are very dependent on the compressor control strategy. In the worst case, a compressor with blow off control might not yield any energy savings with compressed air use reductions, and one with inlet modulation might yield only a small part of potential savings.', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20942, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Reduce compressed air leaks', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20943, 27, 0, 1, 31, 'Compressed air is an expensive utility, but leaks can go uncorrected as they do not make a mess.', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20944, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p>The compressed air leak rate exceeds 20% to 30% of air used in the process.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20945, 27, 0, 1, 8, 'Determine the leak load by checking compressor output when there is no productive use (typically during breaks or after hours.)', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20946, 27, 0, 1, 8, 'Sonic equipment can be used to identify leak locations and estimate associated losses.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20947, 27, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data to Collect</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20948, 27, 0, 1, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-27 22:25:43', 0, '', ''),
(20949, 27, 0, 1, 17, 'An OSU EEC Analysis Template in Microsoft Excel Format', 'vhttps://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1pJoEFwdmULog_SRARRlqzFfzX5cpV6cI', 'Analysis Template: Repair Compressed Air Leaks ', 2, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:08:55', 0, '', ''),
(20950, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Eliminate the use of compressed air “quick fixes” by correcting base issues', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20951, 27, 0, 1, 31, 'Compressed air is a handy utility that can be used for a temporary resolution of miscellaneous production issues, at the cost of expensive air use. Often these fixes persist without correction of the underlying issue.', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20952, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Compressed air used as a temporary quick fix for applications such as cooling bearings, or moving lightweight items that are getting stuck on conveyor.</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20953, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Use alternative to vortex coolers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20954, 27, 0, 1, 31, 'Vortex coolers are an interesting technology that can take a compressed air inlet stream and yield two streams, one that is cold and one that is warm. They are sometimes used to cool electrical cabinets, but in many cases can be replaced with lower energy solutions such as air conditioning or simple fans.', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20955, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Vortex cabinet cooler in use at a facility.</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20956, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Use engineered nozzles for compressed air blow-off applications', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20957, 27, 0, 1, 31, 'Engineered air nozzles can develop effective air flow with a smaller volume of compressed air by entraining atmospheric air in the air stream.', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20958, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Compressed air blowing applications using simple open lines or apertures.</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20959, 27, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data to Collect:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20960, 27, 0, 1, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20961, 27, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Current and proposed pressure requirement</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20962, 27, 0, 1, 14, '<p>Is the current blowing application valved off?</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20963, 27, 0, 1, 4, '<p>This could be a possible source of leaks when not in operation.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20964, 27, 0, 1, 12, '<p>Eliminating the use of compressed air and replacing it with blowers or fans is another viable option for the use of debris removal. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20965, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Serve lower pressure end use with blower or fan', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20966, 27, 0, 1, 31, 'Compressed air is an energy intensive utility with significant heat of compression losses.  These losses can be avoided if the air is not pressurized significantly above that needed for the application. Fans and blowers can develop a like airflow with significantly less energy. ', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20967, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Compressed air used for clearing material, blowing off water, agitating tanks of fluid, or any applications with compressed air regulated to a low pressure</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20968, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Interlock compressed air delivery with equipment or application served.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20969, 27, 0, 1, 31, 'Interlocking a compressed air valve to close when supported equipment is idle can eliminate significant unneeded air use. This can range from an entire packaging line to and isolated ink sprayer that blows air constantly while introducing ink to mark product periodically.', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20970, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Idle equipment with active compressed air blowing applications or leaks</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20971, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Reduce the frequency or duration of intermittent air uses', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20972, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Compressed air used for air bars, bag houses, and similar applications that pulse compressed air.</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20973, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Replace pneumatic hand tools with battery powered hand tools', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20974, 27, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Hand tools are only used intermittently with off hours long enough to charge batteries. </em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20975, 27, 0, 1, 8, '<p>Recommend facility purchase extra batteries to be charging while others are in use. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20976, 27, 0, 1, 2, '<p>Battery powered tools are sometimes not as powerful as air powered options.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20977, 27, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Use desiccant based air dryer with more efficient desiccant bed regeneration.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20978, 27, 0, 0, 11, 'Replace desiccant based air dryer with a refrigerated air dryer if air drying needs permit.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:42:33', 0, '', ''),
(20979, 77, 0, 0, 11, 'Reduce Inlet Air Temperature ', '', '', 1, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20980, 77, 0, 1, 31, 'Reducing the inlet air temperature of oil-injected screw compressors increases mass flow rate while maintaining power input. To efficiently maintain current mass flow rate a variable frequency drive is required to reduce the motor speed and associated power.', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20981, 77, 0, 1, 10, 'High ambient temperature at the air inlet', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20982, 77, 0, 1, 10, 'Difficulty meeting a compressor\'s rated air capacity', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20983, 77, 0, 1, 10, 'A compressor running hotter than its specifications', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20984, 77, 0, 2, 8, 'Other factors may be at play such as significant air leaks increasing the load on the compressor', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20985, 77, 0, 1, 3, '1.9% efficiency (scfm/kW) improvement per 10 °F reduction at inlet', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20986, 77, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data to Collect:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20987, 77, 0, 2, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-27 23:47:09', 0, '', ''),
(20988, 77, 0, 2, 26, 'Average ambient temperature at current and proposed inlet locations', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20989, 77, 0, 1, 12, 'Move air inlet to coolest location to reduce power and energy consumption', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20990, 77, 0, 1, 8, 'If implementation requires much more than re-ducting, the chances of this opportunitity being worthwhile are low. ', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20991, 77, 0, 1, 21, 'An OSU EEC Analysis Template in Microsoft Excel Format', 'https://oregonstate.box.com/s/zk1aol8rf88aul9klflbxkikz6l2ku47', 'Analysis Template: Reduce Inlet Air Temperature', 2, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20992, 77, 0, 1, 17, 'An article from Compressed Air Best Practices by  Tim Dugan, P.E., President, Compression Engineering Corporation', 'https://www.airbestpractices.com/system-assessments/compressor-controls/inlet-air-temperature-impacts-air-compressor-performance', 'Inlet Air Temperature Impacts on Air Compressor Performance', 1, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20993, 77, 0, 0, 11, 'Increase Primary Receiver Capacity', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', '');
INSERT INTO `Items` (`itemId`, `cardId`, `orderIndex`, `indentation`, `iconType`, `contentText`, `contentUrl`, `contentLabel`, `contentMode`, `internal`, `inline`, `sourceId`, `created`, `approved`, `learnMoreUrl`, `integrity`) VALUES
(20994, 77, 0, 1, 31, 'Insufficient receiver capacity can result in short cycling in oil-injected rotary screw compressors that use load-unload controls. Short cycling occurs when system demand forces a compressor to re-load before unload power has been fully realized, causing the compressor to cycle too frequently. Adding receiver capacity increases system efficiency by reducing cycling losses and time spent at partial loads. ', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20995, 77, 0, 1, 10, 'Current receiver capacity for an oil-injected rotary screw compressor is less than 3 gal/cfm', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20996, 77, 0, 1, 10, 'An oil-injected rotary screw compressor consistently unloads for less than 45 seconds', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20997, 77, 0, 1, 3, 'A minimum of 3 gal/cfm receiver capacity is recommended for oil-injected rotary screw compressors ', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20998, 77, 0, 1, 1, 'Improved system efficiency due to reduced cycling frequency ', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(20999, 77, 0, 1, 1, 'Critical pressure applications are shielded from pressure fluctuations', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21000, 77, 0, 1, 1, 'Prevents overloading the compressor\'s motor by allowing for a lower pressure set point ', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21001, 77, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data To Collect:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21002, 77, 0, 2, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21003, 77, 0, 2, 26, 'Current receiver capacity and operating pressure', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21004, 77, 0, 1, 21, 'An OSU EEC Analysis Template in Microsoft Excel Format', 'https://oregonstate.box.com/s/fksaccw3fhif7h70nkynzwlbbu26g608', 'Analysis Template: Increase Air Receiver Capacity', 2, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21005, 77, 0, 1, 20, '', '/uploads/user_42/8bef9996285f82268e4fef3c0c42b38a.png', 'Effect of Receiver Capacity on Lubricant-Injected Rotary Compressor with Load-Unload Capacity Control', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21006, 77, 0, 0, 11, 'Use a more efficient control strategy', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21007, 77, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Many control systems are available for air compressors. Depending on the situation, different control systems can result in the system becoming more efficient.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21008, 77, 0, 1, 32, '', '/uploads/user_60/c10f322f29922e4521e3f5174e19a535.png', '<p>Air Compressor Controls: Performance Profiles</p>', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21009, 77, 0, 1, 31, '<p>The image above is an example of a 200 HP air compressor with a 50% unloading point. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21010, 77, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Start/Stop control system is being used when the process does not require full power all the time. </em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21011, 77, 0, 1, 12, '<p>Consider a Variable Frequency Drive (VFD) control system. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21012, 77, 0, 2, 1, '<p>VFDs modulate output with demand, decreasing unnecessary energy consumption.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21013, 77, 0, 2, 2, '<p>VFDs operate at 103% Full Load Power (FLP) resulting in unnecessary energy consumption when the system is at full capacity. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21014, 77, 0, 1, 8, '<p>VFDs can be retrofit onto an existing system with a small loss in performance if purchasing a new air compressor system is not viable for the facility. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21015, 77, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data to Collect:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21016, 77, 0, 2, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21017, 77, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Current and proposed set point. Include estimated percent of time the set point can be reduced. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21018, 77, 0, 0, 11, 'Use a compressed air sequencer for multiple compressors', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21019, 77, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Running one compressor at full load and the other with a VFD to supplement demand is more efficient than running two air compressors at partial load. The system acts as a \"lead-lag\" scenario where the VFD operates until Full Load Power (FLP) is required, in which case the throttled compressor (compressor 1) would operate using the VFD controlled compressor (compressor 2) to supplement any other compressed air requirements needed above the FLP of compressor 1. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21020, 77, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>System contains more than one air compressor running at less than full load power.</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21021, 77, 0, 1, 4, '<p>VFDs consume 103% of FLP when running at max capacity. If the facility ever needed to run both compressors at max capacity, more energy would be consumed than necessary. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21022, 77, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data to Collect:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21023, 77, 0, 2, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:47:01', 0, '', ''),
(21033, 87, 0, 0, 11, 'Capture heat rejected by air compressors', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21034, 87, 0, 1, 10, '<p><em>Air compressor room is nearby a heated space (i.e. an office).</em></p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21035, 87, 0, 1, 8, '<p>The viability of this recommendation is primarily dependent on the current heating system and length of heating season. </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21036, 87, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Data to Collect:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21037, 87, 0, 2, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-324', 'Standard Data', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21038, 87, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Annual heating hours</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21039, 87, 0, 2, 26, '<p>HVAC target temperature.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21040, 87, 0, 1, 21, '<p>An OSU EEC analysis template in Microsoft Excel Format.</p>', 'https://oregonstate.app.box.com/file/298053373341', 'Recover Air Compressor Heat ', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21041, 87, 0, 0, 11, 'Replace refrigerated compressed air dryer with more efficient refrigerated compressed air dryer', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 15:51:09', 0, '', ''),
(21053, 306, 0, 0, 31, '<p>The overall efficiency of hydraulic actuation systems is lower than an electrically driven systems because energy changes its form more often. However, hydraulic systems are favorable or required in some specific applications.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:21:40', 0, '', ''),
(21054, 306, 0, 0, 1, '<p>reduced energy consumption</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:21:40', 0, '', ''),
(21055, 306, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Electrically driven systems may require less maintenance. There is no need to replace worn out hydraulic components and to retune control systems. There is also no risk of leakages from hoses, pipes, tanks, valves or pumps.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:21:40', 0, '', ''),
(21056, 306, 0, 0, 2, '<p>Electric systems have lower power density. Hydraulic actuators develop large torque for comparatively small devices.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:21:40', 0, '', ''),
(21057, 306, 0, 0, 2, '<p>It is dangerous to operate an electric motor continuously at full load and low speed</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:21:40', 0, '', ''),
(21058, 306, 0, 0, 26, '<p>check hydraulics AR in OR720</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:21:40', 0, '', ''),
(21062, 314, 0, 0, 24, '<p></p>', 'https://www.plantservices.com/articles/2004/444/?page=full', 'Reduce costs with variable speed drives', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:22:59', 0, '', ''),
(21063, 314, 0, 0, 31, '<p>I am struggling how best to cover Variable Speed Drives: within the motors page, within the motors overview, in its own heading like this. Besides Solid State VSDs there are other technologies (seldom seen) like hydraulics, eddy clutches, etc.)</p>', '', '', 1, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:22:59', 0, '', ''),
(21064, 314, 0, 0, 31, '<p>develop introduction for VFDs, include any VFD templates as internal resources, link to any other VFD recommendations from this page</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-12 18:22:59', 0, '', ''),
(21277, 163, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Aeration is a common process used in conventional wastewater treatment plants. Air is supplied to the influent wastewater to promote the aerobic degradation of organic matter via oxygen metabolizing microbes.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 33, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21278, 163, 0, 1, 7, '<p>Integrated systems that match air supply to demand in the influent wastewater are the most efficient.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21279, 163, 0, 1, 27, '<p>Power Quality Analyzer, Data Loggers, Vane Anemometer </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21280, 163, 0, 0, 11, 'Replace Standard Aeration Fans with High Efficiency Turbo Blowers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21281, 163, 0, 1, 10, '<p>WWTP using outdated equipment.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21282, 163, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Blower nameplate/motor nameplate</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21283, 163, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Flow rates, inlet pressure, outlet pressure, live amperage data</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21284, 163, 0, 1, 17, '<p>Example recommendation for replacing existing blowers with a more efficient model.</p>', 'https://oregonstate.app.box.com/file/723752040170', 'Install Efficienct Blowers', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 18:17:21', 0, '', ''),
(21285, 163, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Install VFD control on Aeration Blowers</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21286, 163, 0, 1, 31, '<p>WWTPs can experience 5 factor load fluctuations over a 24-hour period. Poor control of aeration can result in excess air being supplied during lower loads, causing excess energy consumption by as much as 50 - 65 %.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 33, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21287, 163, 0, 1, 10, '<p>Aeration blowers manually throttled or supplying excess air to the process.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21288, 163, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Allows for efficient operation over a wide range of flow conditions.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21289, 163, 0, 1, 2, '<p>VFDs are expensive to install - becoming cheaper in recent years.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21290, 163, 0, 1, 4, '<p>VFDs can harm the motor if they are not properly installed.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21291, 163, 0, 1, 14, '<p>Would downsizing the blower(s) result in additional savings?</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21292, 163, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Blower nameplate/motor nameplate</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21293, 163, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Flow rates, inlet pressure, outlet pressure, live amperage data</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21294, 163, 0, 1, 17, '<p>Example recommendation for replacing broken variable frequency drives on aeration blowers.</p>', 'https://oregonstate.app.box.com/file/721822365546', 'Replace VFDs on Blowers', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21295, 163, 0, 0, 11, 'Control Aeration to Hold a Minimum Dissolved Oxygen Level', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21296, 163, 0, 1, 10, '<p>WWTPs may supply more air than necessary to aeration basins if they are not monitoring oxygen levels.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21297, 163, 0, 1, 4, '<p>It is critical for a plant to supply enough aeration to provide effective contaminant removal. Care should be taken to ensure that reductions in air supplied will still allow the plant to meet treatment targets.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21298, 163, 0, 1, 2, '<p>Manually controlling aeration is difficult to do and is less efficient than an automated system (see opportunities below).</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21299, 163, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Install Dissolved Oxygen Probes</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21300, 163, 0, 1, 1, '<p>DO probes allow for accurate tracking of oxygen content in the influent wastewater so aeration can be adjusted accordingly.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21301, 163, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Automatic Dissolved Oxygen Controls</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21302, 163, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Automated DO sensors can be integrated to the aeration system to control blower flow based on influent demand.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21303, 163, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Automatic controls remove the need for staff to manually monitor and adjust the supplied air.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21304, 163, 0, 1, 7, '<p>Utilizing system control strategies such as SCADA allow for complete automation of an aeration system.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21305, 163, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Improve Efficiency with Fine Bubble Diffusers</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21306, 163, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Fine bubble diffusers offer increased oxygen transfer efficiency (OTE) over course bubble.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21307, 163, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Aeration with Pure Oxygen</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21308, 163, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Increases the capacity of the existing aeration system, reducing associated energy costs.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21309, 163, 0, 1, 2, '<p>Requires the purchase of oxygen gas to use.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21310, 163, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Aerating with pure oxygen may be particularly suitable if the plant is having trouble meeting treatment requirements, or has excessively high power costs.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:09:29', 0, '', ''),
(21319, 175, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Install Anaerobic Digester</p>', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:25:57', 0, '', ''),
(21320, 175, 0, 0, 17, '<p>Example recommendation for installing an anaerobic digester and equipment required to convert biogas from manure to usable methane.</p>', 'https://oregonstate.app.box.com/file/297830530132', 'Install Anaerobic Digester', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 18:16:56', 0, '', ''),
(21321, 175, 0, 0, 11, 'Use digester gas in a dual fuel boiler', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:25:57', 0, '', ''),
(21322, 175, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Biogas formed during anaerobic digestion can be used in on-site boilers to provide process, space, and water heating.</p>', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 33, '2021-05-23 20:25:57', 0, '', ''),
(21323, 175, 0, 0, 11, 'Clean and concentrate digester gas for sale to natural gas utility', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:25:57', 0, '', ''),
(21324, 175, 0, 0, 24, '<p>This slideshow for the Better Plants Program covers the benefits of biogas for Water/Wastewater treatment plants.</p>', 'https://betterbuildingssolutioncenter.energy.gov/sites/default/files/Beneficial%20Use%20of%20Biogas%20part%201_0.pdf', 'Beneficial Use of Biogas Part 1', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:25:57', 0, '', ''),
(21325, 175, 0, 0, 24, '<p>This slideshow for the Better Plants Program covers the benefits of biogas for Water/Wastewater treatment plants.</p>', 'https://betterbuildingssolutioncenter.energy.gov/sites/default/files/Beneficial%20Use%20of%20Biogas%20part%202_1.pdf', 'Benfeficial Use of Biogas Part 2', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-23 20:25:57', 0, '', ''),
