(21666, 272, 0, 0, 11, 'Recover heat rejected from condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21667, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Often, heat rejected from the condensers can be used to heat a nearby process stream, lowering the associated heating load.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21668, 272, 0, 1, 10, 'A low-temperature process is located nearby water-cooled condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21669, 272, 0, 2, 12, '<p>Install split condensers to reduce the cooling tower load. A split condenser first uses a nearby process stream to precool the refrigerant before it enters a second condenser that uses cooling tower water.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21670, 272, 0, 1, 3, '14,500 Btu/hr per ton produced is rejected in the condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21671, 272, 0, 0, 15, '<p>Data to collect</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21672, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Refrigeration capacity (tons)', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21673, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Temperature of refrigerant entering the condensers', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21674, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Temperature of the process stream to be heated', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21675, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Mass flow rates of refrigerant and process stream', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21676, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Refrigerant and process fluid properties', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21677, 272, 0, 0, 11, 'Insulate hot/cold surfaces', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21678, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Un-insulated cold/hot lines or tanks create unnecessary heat transfer and can result in large energy losses. Simply adding appropriate insulation on these surfaces will result in substantial energy savings.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21679, 272, 0, 1, 33, '<p></p>', '#card-130', 'See Insulation on the Thermal Systems page for more information', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21680, 272, 0, 0, 11, 'Use hot gas defrost', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21681, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p><em class=\"ql-size-small\">Lets talk about this one.- Joe</em></p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21682, 272, 0, 1, 31, '<p>When air cooling units operate below 32 ºF, frost inevitably builds up on evaporator coils. Frost acts as an insulator and hinders heat exchanger performance. As a result, a defrost cycle must be implemented for these systems.</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21683, 272, 0, 1, 12, 'Cycle hot refrigerant from the compressor discharge through the evaporator coils to melt frost.', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21684, 272, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Heats coils from the inside so less heat is transferred to the surrounding air</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21685, 272, 0, 1, 2, '<p>More complex system design and higher implementation cost</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21686, 272, 0, 1, 3, 'Savings will generally be on the order of 10-20% of the total system use', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21687, 272, 0, 1, 4, '<p>Suitable only for larger systems with multiple evaporators. In order to use hot gas, the system needs to produce it. While one evaporator is defrosting the others will run; at least two to three evaporators running for each evaporator defrosting is required for low-moderate temperature systems.</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21688, 272, 0, 0, 15, '<p>Data to collect</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21689, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Defrost cycle schedule ', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21690, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Power of the current electric defrost system', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(21691, 272, 0, 1, 26, 'Distance from compressor discharge to evaporators to determine the amount of piping required', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 20:27:35', 1, '', ''),
(22033, 131, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Cooling towers use evaporative cooling in atmospheric conditions to achieve wet bulb temperatures (below dry bulb temperatures) for a circulated water system. Circulation between a heat source and a cooling tower through a cooling medium (such as water) allows excess heat to be expelled to the atmosphere.</p><p>Cooling towers may be used as standalone equipment or added to a chiller system to reduce the load when outside conditions are favorable. There are three common types of cooling towers used today: forced-draft, induced-draft, and hyperbolic (natural draft).</p><p>Industrial refrigeration commonly uses a cooling tower at the condenser, to bring refrigerant to a lower condensing temperature/pressure, reducing the work required by the refrigeration compressor. Cooling towers can also be used to recycle water in quenching and cooling processes where chilled water heated by the process might otherwise be disposed of.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22034, 131, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Perhaps explain </p><p>- forced-draft vs induced vs natural and when it might matter</p><p>- differences between an open (water) and closed (water/glycol) loop system</p><p>- wet vs dry system. </p><p></p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22035, 131, 0, 0, 20, '', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Counterflow_diagram.svg/571px-Counterflow_diagram.svg.png', '<p>How a cooling tower functions</p>', 0, 0, 0, 31, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22036, 131, 0, 0, 11, 'Install a cooling tower to reduce the chiller load.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22037, 131, 0, 1, 10, '<p>High utilization of chilled water or process water used for cooling.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22038, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Equipment operating hours</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22039, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Cooling medium properties</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22040, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Specific heat</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22041, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Incoming cooling tower temperature </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22042, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Target cooling temperature</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22043, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Cooling medium (glycol, water, etc.)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22044, 131, 0, 1, 27, '<p>Power quality analyzer (to evaluate chiller load)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22045, 131, 0, 1, 1, '<p>Cooling towers can function under some weather conditions without fan power, greatly reducing energy consumption due to \"free cooling\".</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22046, 131, 0, 1, 2, '<p>Cooling towers require large spaces typically on rooftops to function well.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22047, 131, 0, 1, 4, '<p>Cooling towers need to be carefully monitored in winter climates where water may freeze inside the tower.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22048, 131, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Install variable frequency drives (VFDs) on cooling tower fans</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22049, 131, 0, 1, 10, '<p>High usage cooling towers or those with varying flows/loads not currently utilizing VFDs</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22050, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Fan motor nameplate data</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22051, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Fan motor live power readings</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22052, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Operation hours</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22053, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Load factors throughout the year, either estimated or datalogged</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22054, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Load factors should be estimated as \"X% for Y%\" of the year due to cooling tower performance being weather dependent. A cooling tower running at 50% of capacity at the time of measurement cannot be assumed to be representative of an entire year unless specifically stated otherwise by facility personnel.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22055, 131, 0, 1, 27, '<p>Power quality analyzer</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22056, 131, 0, 1, 3, '<p>Power consumption and fan speed have a cubic relationship, meaning even small reductions in fan speed can have high energy savings.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22057, 131, 0, 1, 1, '<p>VFDs offer higher energy savings in flow reduction than inlet vanes and outlet dampers.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22058, 131, 0, 1, 2, '<p>The initial cost of VFDs can lead to high payback periods for low use equipment.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22059, 131, 0, 1, 2, '<p>Energy savings are only realized for fans running at partial loads</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22060, 131, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Reduce cooling tower fan speed</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22061, 131, 0, 1, 31, '<p>Add link to FCAT</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22062, 131, 0, 1, 31, '<p>kind of left wondering when one would choose to operate at say 80% vs 70% if the impact on performance is small either way and the energy savings would be much greater at 70%. </p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22063, 131, 0, 1, 10, '<p>Cooling tower fans set to constant speeds year round or set to full speed.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22064, 131, 0, 1, 3, '<p>Required fan power varies with the cube of the speed. For instance: if the fan is dropped to 50% speed, the power will drop to 12.5% of full load power (0.5 x 0.5 x 0.5 = 0.125)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22065, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Fan motor nameplate data</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22066, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Fan motor live power readings</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22067, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Operation hours</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22068, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Load factors throughout the year, either estimated or datalogged</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22069, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Load factors should be estimated as \"X% for Y%\" of the year due to cooling tower performance being weather dependent. A cooling tower running at 50% of capacity at the time of measurement cannot be assumed to be representative of an entire year unless specifically stated otherwise by facility personnel.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22070, 131, 0, 1, 27, '<p>Power quality analyzer</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22071, 131, 0, 1, 8, '<p>Cooling towers may be used as standalone equipment or added to a chiller system to reduce the load when outside conditions are ideal. There are three common types of cooling towers used today: forced-draft, induced-draft, and hyperbolic (natural draft).</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22072, 131, 0, 1, 8, '<p>Cooling tower models based on manufacturer data show that reducing fan speeds to as low as  60% capacity has little impact on cooling tower performance, with larger performance degradation beginning below 50%</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 32, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22073, 131, 0, 1, 12, '<p>Reduce cooling tower fan speed incrementally and monitor equipment for unanticipated or adverse effects.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22074, 131, 0, 0, 11, '<p>Utilize cooling towers to bypass chillers in cooler weather</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22075, 131, 0, 1, 10, '<p>Facilities with cooling towers in cooler climates or that experience cooler seasons.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22076, 131, 0, 1, 1, '<p>A closed circuit cooling tower system can produce water cool enough to bypass a chiller and be used directly for process water, also known as \"free cooling\".</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22077, 131, 0, 1, 3, '<p>Free cooling can be utilized in systems where the outdoor wet bulb temperature is 2 °F lower than the desired process temperature.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22078, 131, 0, 1, 27, '<p>Sling psychrometer</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22079, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Desired cooling tower outlet temperature.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22080, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Ambient wet bulb over the year, or period of interest. Data can often be obtained on-line</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22081, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p> Cooling tower inlet temperature logged or estimated for a year.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22082, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Cooling Tower Approach Temperature. Evaluate by comparing simultaneous:</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22083, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Wet bulb temperature (using your sling psychrometer)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22084, 131, 0, 2, 26, '<p>Cooling tower water exit temperature</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22085, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Cooling tower operating hours</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22086, 131, 0, 1, 15, '<p>Chiller energy usage logged or estimated for a year</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:04:52', 1, '', ''),
(22106, 340, 0, 0, 25, '<p>Pacific NW Boiler Vendor</p>', 'https://coleindust.com/', 'Cole Industrial', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:21:14', 1, '', ''),
(22107, 340, 0, 0, 25, '<p>Pacific NW Boiler Vendor</p>', 'https://www.nationwideboiler.com/pacific-combustion-engineering.html', 'Pacific Combustion Engineering', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:21:14', 1, '', ''),
(22108, 340, 0, 0, 25, '<p>Boiler Manufacturer</p>', 'http://cleaverbrooks.com/', 'CleaverBrooks', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-01 22:28:20', 1, '', ''),
(22121, 88, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Steam systems are versatile, a long established technology, and a familiar utility for many industrial personnel.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:26:06', 1, '', ''),
(22122, 88, 0, 0, 1, 'A single thermal energy input at the boiler can be distributed throughout a facility.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:26:06', 1, '', ''),
(22123, 88, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Serving thermal applications with steam instead of different combustion processes reduces administrative cost associated with managing and reporting multiple emissions sources to governing agencies.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:26:06', 1, '', ''),
(22124, 88, 0, 1, 26, '<p>Thermal needs can be served by a dual fuel boiler (eg: one that can use either natural gas or fuel oil) can reduce vulnerability to outages and allow a facility to purchase less expensive fuel on an interruptible rate schedule. End uses served by this steam instead of a local fuel combustion process will be protected.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:26:06', 1, '', ''),
(22125, 88, 0, 0, 1, 'Steam engines can be useful for applications that might result in an initial locked rotor and potential electric motor damage, such as pumping cold semi-solidified bunker fuel.', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:26:06', 1, '', ''),
(22126, 88, 0, 0, 1, '<p>Boilers often allow multiple fuel sources, making them more resilient to utility grid disruptions.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:26:06', 1, '', ''),
(22134, 315, 0, 0, 17, '<p>This checklist was prepared in collaboration with and funded by the Bonneville Power Administration in 1998.</p>', 'https://eec.oregonstate.edu/sites/eec.oregonstate.edu/files/walkthrough_checklist.pdf', 'The Industrial Walkthrough Checklist', 3, 0, 0, 0, '2021-05-26 22:32:28', 0, '', 'sha384-Ly07df2GKGl4DiyXQmesKjrDMtbXmRkWJQa7DurCI0+pjSSi8HaXsgJBCnXjJEm3'),
