(23749, 364, 0, 0, 31, '<p>For the production of beer, four different vessels are typically required in order to break down the complex carbohydrates of the initial beer ingredients into the simple sugars that form the finished product. First, the malt is crushed and ground in a mill, and a part of it is added with water into a mash kettle, or boiler. The remainder of the malt is added to the second vessel, the mash tun, along with superheated water, and let to sit. Once the material in the mash kettle begins to boil, it\'s moved to the mash tun in order to quickly increase the temperature and control the enzymes. The mash is then transferred to a lauter tun, or strainer, in order to collect the simple carbohydrates. The refined mash and hops are added to another boiler, and then sent into a whirlpool separator. This vessel uses centrifugal force to separate out the hot ingredients. The remaining solution is moved into a fermentation chamber, where it undergoes chemical reactions, and then refermented for maximum purity. Once aged for the requisite amount of time, the beer is filtered and stored.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 39, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23750, 364, 1, 0, 20, '', '/uploads/user_82/e4f996ddf9eafb20e79e86220fd87ad4.png', '<p>Brewingasdf</p>', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23751, 364, 2, 0, 23, '<p></p>', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ePzRpzohx1Y', 'Beer Production Overview', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23752, 364, 3, 0, 23, '<p></p>', 'https://www.britannica.com/video/186957/chemistry-beer-brewmaster-process-Boston-Massachusetts-Samuel', 'Ingredients and Fermentation in the Brewing Process', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23753, 364, 4, 0, 31, '<p>Process Units Include:</p>', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 39, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23754, 364, 5, 1, 26, '<p>Boiler</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23755, 364, 6, 2, 21, '<p></p>', 'https://walkthrough.eec.oregonstate.edu/wiki/technologies/46', 'EEC Boiler Page', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23756, 364, 7, 1, 26, '<p>Separator</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 40, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23757, 364, 8, 2, 31, '<p>Separators filter out desired products from less desirable byproducts. For instance, separators take the liquid version of ammonia after it has been run through a heat exchanger and remove it from the raw, unconverted gases. This differs from a filter as the undesired products can still be reintegrated into the system rather than removed.</p>', '', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23758, 364, 9, 1, 26, '<p>Filter</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 40, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23759, 364, 10, 2, 31, '<p>Filters use a system of high and low pressure and a semi-porous barrier to isolate desired materials. The differing pressures allow the substance to flow, and the barrier, typically containing sand or other small semi-porous material, separates out the smaller product. Once the larger material saturates the filter, it requires maintenance.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23760, 364, 11, 1, 26, '<p>Fermenter</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-16 20:50:21', 0, '', ''),
(23767, 241, 0, 0, 31, '<p>Upon completion of a remote guided tour, the assessment team will meet to determine which opportunities should be pursued.</p>', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:15:02', 0, '', ''),
(23768, 241, 1, 0, 31, '<p>If possible, this meeting should include the client.</p>', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:15:02', 0, '', ''),
(23809, 156, 0, 0, 31, '<p>This meeting is analogous to the what the OSU IAC has traditionally called the \"Pre-Audit Walkthrough Phone Call\" (excluding site visit logistics, safety and PPE discussion)</p>', '%zXz%', '%zXz%', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23810, 156, 1, 0, 26, '<p>Have the client(s) verbally  \"walk us through\" their process, highlighting key energy intensive processes</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23811, 156, 2, 1, 14, '<p>Ask client(s) to let us know of any areas of concern or interest</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23812, 156, 3, 1, 14, '<p>Ask for rated capacity, estimated % of full capacity, and hours of operation for significant equipment discussed.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23813, 156, 4, 2, 8, '<p>Estimates of the number of smaller motor of various sizes with average load and hours can also be helpful.</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23814, 156, 5, 1, 14, '<p>Are common utilities such as compressed air, lighting, heating, etc covered in the conversation?</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23815, 156, 6, 0, 26, '<p>Discuss proposed process for remote assessment going forward (we are still learning and developing this process)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23816, 156, 7, 0, 8, '<p>Try to get more than one key contact at the site involved in the project. (Plant manager, Fiscal Decision Maker, Maintenance Manager, Floor Personnel, Energy Lead, etc)</p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23817, 156, 8, 0, 17, '<p>(Item not added yet)</p>', 'abc.com', 'Pre-Audit Walkthrough Phone Call Checklist', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23818, 156, 9, 0, 14, '<p>How best could we get Utility &amp; Incentive Representatives involved (if the client permits) </p>', '', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
(23819, 156, 10, 0, 26, '<p>At this point, an analyst should be assigned to start the general background. It may take more time to develop the general background while doing a remote assessment so it\'s best to start it early.</p>', '', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, '2026-04-21 00:37:16', 1, '', ''),
