INSERT INTO `Requests` (`requestId`, `title`, `description`, `status`, `created`, `userId`) VALUES
(5, 'Metals Manufacturing', 'This is the metals manufacturing page that I started while working with ColMac', 4, '2020-10-15 18:21:13', 52),
(6, 'Utility Billing - Electricity', 'This introduces the utilities page and covers electricity billing structure.  Other utilities are to follow in a similar fashion, so I\'m wanting to check organization and content before reviewing any others.  Last note:  I have no idea what picture to put for the page, so very much open to any suggestions. Thanks!', 2, '2020-10-16 22:04:13', 54),
(11, 'Refrigeration opportunity - reduce system lift', 'Two methods for reducing system lift are included: increase suction pressure and decrease discharge pressure. ', 4, '2020-12-16 01:40:52', 58),
(12, 'Refrigeration Opportunity: Reduce System Lift', 'A card containing two methods for reducing system lift: increase suction pressure and decrease discharge pressure.', 4, '2020-12-16 01:43:02', 58),
(13, 'Refrigeration Page', 'Brief summary of industrial refrigeration systems and design factors to consider. ', 4, '2020-12-16 01:45:12', 58),
(14, 'Pump Page', 'Quite a bit of content related to pumps in general as well as a couple of opportunities.', 4, '2020-12-19 00:49:42', 55),
(15, 'Boiler and Steam', 'Updates to add additional descriptions to some recommendations. \nSeveral items contain minor grammar changes.\nChanges some of the resources from public to internal, as they require access to OSU box folders', 4, '2020-12-20 02:12:40', 61),
(16, 'Thermal Systems Overview', 'The overview, useful links, pros, cons, and best practices.', 4, '2020-12-21 20:35:42', 57),
(20, 'How to create KaTeX formulas', 'An internal page that shows editors how to create KaTeX formulas.', 4, '2021-01-10 23:48:46', 42),
(21, 'Thermal Systems - Heat Exchangers', 'Just the heat exchanger section, not the others.', 4, '2021-01-15 19:20:58', 57),
(23, 'Utility Billing - Analysis', 'This section explains the benefits, beginning approach, and FAQs relating to analyzing utility bills.', 2, '2021-02-10 19:24:01', 54),
(24, 'How to develop this application', 'Easy to access page that explains to new developers some basics of getting started.', 4, '2021-02-11 00:50:23', 42),
(25, 'Cooling towers', 'The entire card', 3, '2021-03-29 22:39:51', 57),
(26, 'Boilers and Steam Templet Links', 'Added and updated links to templets', 4, '2021-04-29 23:35:10', 61),
(27, 'Wastewater ', 'Some general info, additional resource links, and opportunity cards.', 4, '2021-05-11 16:47:34', 55),
(28, 'Compressed Air - Reduce Pressure', 'BR is Matt', 2, '2021-05-24 17:52:47', 60),
(29, 'Compressed Air - Reduce Compressed Air Required', 'BR is Ryan', 4, '2021-05-24 17:55:31', 60),
(30, 'Compressed Air - Reduce Pressure Required', 'BR is Ryan', 2, '2021-05-24 17:57:23', 60),
(31, 'Compressed Air - improve Efficiency ', 'BR is Matt', 2, '2021-05-24 17:58:21', 60),
(32, 'Example', 'Please review such and such', 4, '2021-05-26 21:13:44', 58),
(33, 'Test', 'Example', 4, '2021-05-26 22:10:54', 58),
(34, 'Test', 'Test', 4, '2021-07-28 18:30:00', 61);
INSERT INTO `Request_Comments` (`commentId`, `requestId`, `targetId`, `comment`, `review`, `created`, `userId`) VALUES
(31, 5, 'C214', '<p>I know what you are talking about when you mention ovens (paint booths that also can be used as curing oven) but the idea should be introduced somehow. </p>', 0, '2020-11-03 21:12:22', 51),
(32, 5, 'C214', '<p>Cast ROT in imperial units as well</p>', 0, '2020-11-03 21:14:45', 51),
(33, 5, 'C214', '<p>Two items to add. We often suggest occupancy sensors on Paint Booths to turn them off after a set period of inactivity. We also have focused on ensuring the high intensity lighting is also off when not needed. </p>', 0, '2020-11-03 21:18:45', 51),
(34, 5, 'C212', '<p>Should mention that over spray reduction can also reduce need to replace paint booth air filters and associated material and waste costs. </p>', 0, '2020-11-03 21:22:20', 51),
(35, 5, 'C213', '<p>Hmm, I like the ETO information, but we should identify that it is a local opportunity somehow. Perhaps it should start as a suggestion to check on potential incentives with ETO as an example. (Makes me think we should create a specific bullet for incentives (and cost?) information </p>', 0, '2020-11-03 21:23:58', 51),
(36, 5, 'C213', '<p>We need to identify the energy cost used in the estimate of savings for upgrading a single transformer-rectifier welder</p>', 0, '2020-11-03 21:29:01', 51),
(37, 5, 'C215', '<p>We should add hot link to the compressed air section</p>', 0, '2020-11-03 21:30:49', 51),
(38, 5, '0', '<p>LMSA: Wanted to move this along ;-) And use this review function more to see if anything needs to change. I have a power point  I will send you. We should add any opportunities in the power point that are not here but specific to metals. </p>', 1, '2020-11-03 21:53:55', 51),
(39, 12, '0', '<p>I would put a pressure-enthalpy chart somewhere on the page so that there is a visual \"this is suction, this is discharge, and this is what lift looks like\" indication. I think that would make it more clear for someone familiar with refrigeration, but maybe confused about the wording.</p>', 1, '2020-12-17 19:55:40', 57),
(40, 12, '0', '<p>\"If fan savings are unavailable the suction pressure should be set as high as possible.\" is unclear to me. Would this not increase fan power? How does this help?</p>', 0, '2020-12-17 19:57:26', 57),
(41, 12, '0', '<p>Clarify what a compressor operational profile is. Energy use over time? Operating hours? Control scheme? Similarly, explain stuff like float.</p><p><br></p><p>I think the page is mostly good, but needs clarification in some of the technical stuff. Maybe this doesn\'t fit on the card, but something higher on the page explaining the importance of pressure in the refrigeration cycle, what float is, where in the cycle suction and discharge pressures play their respective roles, etc. That would make things much better on the page.</p>', 0, '2020-12-17 20:04:58', 57),
(42, 13, '0', '<p>\"such as air and water\" instead of \"typically air and water\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>', 1, '2020-12-17 20:10:09', 57),
(43, 13, '0', '<p>\"Improving the energy efficiency of such systems not only reduces energy consumption, but can often reduce labor costs and improve productivity, product quality, and system reliability.\"</p><p><br></p><p>how? explain</p>', 0, '2020-12-17 20:10:33', 57),
(44, 14, 'C82', '<p>\"Replace Valve Control with<em><u> Variable Speed Drive</u></em> Control\"</p><p>For the rest of the page VSD is referred to as VFD. While the terms are almost interchangeable, I think it would be less confusing to pick one term to use, unless otherwise stated.   </p>', 1, '2020-12-19 18:10:09', 61),
(45, 14, 'C84', '<p>What is the \"Least Closed Valve Strategy\"? </p><p>A short description would be very helpful for someone who is not familiar with pumps.</p>', 1, '2020-12-19 18:22:40', 61),
(46, 14, 'C82', '<p>Data to collect section should be near the recommendation instead of at the bottom</p>', 1, '2020-12-19 18:29:50', 61),
(47, 14, '0', '<p>Overall the page looks good. Headers and recommendation titles are clear. Page is nicely organized by sections. Benefits and drawback are highlighted. Important information is included.</p><p>I would suggest that the Gallery card is made internal until the pictures are put in.</p><p>I suggest looking at the pump overview section. It looks like the cards are out of order. I was thinking that the data collection should be at top, and links at bottom.</p>', 2, '2020-12-19 18:44:06', 61),
(48, 15, 'C96', '<p>Changed so that the two measuring equipment were on separate lines</p>', 0, '2020-12-20 02:55:21', 61),
(49, 15, 'C97', '<p>Changed to internal reference</p>', 0, '2020-12-20 02:55:55', 61),
(50, 15, 'C98', '<p>Changed to internal reference</p>', 0, '2020-12-20 02:56:32', 61),
(51, 15, 'C101', '<p>Changed Template to internal reference.</p>', 0, '2020-12-20 02:58:16', 61),
(52, 15, 'C101', '<p>This card is very full. Any suggestions about splitting up the card or removing items?</p>', 0, '2020-12-20 02:59:00', 61),
(53, 15, 'C103', '<p>This description was borrowed from an old EEC guide book. </p><p>It seems good, but is it too much?</p>', 0, '2020-12-20 03:01:57', 61),
(54, 15, 'C105', '<p>Any additional items needed for \"Fix faulty steam traps\"?</p>', 0, '2020-12-20 03:03:22', 61),
(55, 16, 'P47', '<p>change \"focus\" to \"focuses\"</p>', 0, '2020-12-22 00:57:07', 55),
(56, 16, 'P47', '<p>change \"Often times\" to \"Often\"</p>', 0, '2020-12-22 00:58:40', 55),
(57, 16, 'C261', '<ul><li>maybe reword \"reducing generation costs\" this is a bit unclear</li><li>remove first \"equipment\" from from fourth pro</li><li>change \"cheaper\" to \"cheap\"</li></ul>', 0, '2020-12-22 01:05:22', 55),
(58, 16, 'C262', '<p>add \"often\" prior to \"requiring non-generic quotes and high costs\"</p><p>change \"in consideration\" to \"to consider\" in the second sentence of the first bullet</p>', 0, '2020-12-22 01:07:54', 55),
(59, 16, '0', '<p>Overall looks good. I think you got quite a bit of important information in there. Links are great. I suggested a few changes to the wording but it all looks nice!</p>', 0, '2020-12-22 01:10:53', 55),
(62, 16, '0', '<p>Thanks Julian!</p>', 2, '2021-01-12 21:13:10', 57),
(63, 21, 'C129', '<p>Consider switching the red flags and description text boxes</p>', 1, '2021-02-10 01:35:00', 58),
(64, 21, 'C129', '<p>The figures included here are good examples of HEs but may not be widely helpful. Instead you could include diagrams of common HE styles and do a bit of comparison. Maybe there is a better place on the page for that though, in which case you could just link to that section. </p>', 0, '2021-02-10 01:38:57', 58),
(65, 21, 'C129', '<p><strong>Data to Collect</strong></p><p></p><p>Temps?</p><p></p><p>Maybe compile all fluid property data (density, specific heat, others that are used in the analysis) into an indented bulleted list below the fluid properties item</p>', 0, '2021-02-10 01:48:52', 58),
(66, 21, 'C129', '<p>Cool sludge report!</p>', 0, '2021-02-10 01:49:38', 58),
(67, 21, 'H40', '<p>I don\'t think I\'ve ever done a heat exchanger AR, if you know of any good past fluid-to-fluid ars let me know and I\'ll work on getting a template approved. Pre-heat comb. air is on the way</p>', 0, '2021-02-10 01:52:12', 58),
(69, 21, '0', '<p>Overall the card looks good, at some point other types of heat exchangers can be added</p>', 2, '2021-02-10 01:57:30', 58),
(70, 13, '0', '<p>Ryan, I went through the page and published a fair bit and left a few comments as internal items .</p>', 2, '2021-02-10 19:47:02', 51),
(71, 13, '0', '<p>Ditto</p>', 3, '2021-02-10 19:47:16', 51),
(72, 14, '0', '<p>Julian, I went through. made some edits and published most of the page. I left a few placeholder cards you had added unpublished. </p>', 0, '2021-02-10 19:49:33', 51),
(73, 14, '0', '<p>Neglected to mark it reviewed.</p>', 3, '2021-02-10 19:50:20', 51),
(74, 5, 'C211', '<p>[aoRIHHASORIF</p>', 0, '2021-02-11 21:45:23', 51),
(75, 24, '0', '<p>Fine start on this for us to work forward from.</p>', 2, '2021-02-17 21:23:46', 51),
(76, 24, '0', '<p>;-)</p>', 3, '2021-02-17 21:24:03', 51),
(77, 6, '0', '<p>For the photo maybe a stock photo of a substation? The one in place works too</p>', 0, '2021-02-23 01:15:22', 58),
(78, 6, 'C223', '<p>Maybe make the \"consult your provided rate sch..\" item a tip or suggested action</p>', 1, '2021-02-23 01:16:34', 58),
(79, 6, 'C224', '<p>I think you can remove \"of\" after application</p>', 1, '2021-02-23 01:19:29', 58),
(80, 6, '0', '<p></p>', 2, '2021-02-23 01:21:35', 58),
(81, 23, 'C294', '<p>The first sentence reads a little awkward to me, maybe go with something like \"Analyzing utilities is an excellent way to quantify total energy use, identify where energy is used, and reveal trends that are not readily apparent from individual billing statements alone. </p>', 1, '2021-02-23 01:26:06', 58),
(82, 23, 'C295', '<p>Add our utility analysis template </p>', 0, '2021-02-23 01:30:18', 58),
(83, 23, 'C276', '<p>Can you explain more how the provider purchasing the utility as a commodity results in a lower cost? My economics knowledge is ahem... minimal</p>', 0, '2021-02-23 01:37:48', 58),
(84, 23, 'C276', '<p>Link directly to Power Factor Correction page</p>', 1, '2021-02-23 01:38:26', 58),
(85, 23, '0', '<p>In general you may be able to make more use of all the different item icons and potentially add more resources/graphics. That said, I appreciate the clean look of the page too. </p>', 0, '2021-02-23 01:42:28', 58),
(86, 23, '0', '<p>Nice work!</p>', 2, '2021-02-23 01:42:43', 58),
(87, 21, 'C129', '<p>Consider rewording the heat exchange paragraph at the start. Maybe \"The benefits of a heat exchanger between hot and cold streams can be twofold\"</p>', 1, '2021-03-04 00:42:42', 55),
(88, 21, 'C129', '<p>Concurrent flow heat exchangers can actually be more effective than counter current due to the larger initial temp difference as a driving force. But they are more energy intensive (way more flow) and I think might require bigger exchangers. Maybe just note that counter current are the most common and applicable to industry in general, but other configurations exist</p>', 0, '2021-03-04 00:46:45', 55),
(89, 21, 'C129', '<p>Maybe more applicable to the thermal systems page in general but it would be good to get information about condensing heat exchangers vs two fluids with no phase change. Then obviously talking about the dangers associated with condensing or vaporizing a bunch of steam in these systems. </p>', 0, '2021-03-04 00:51:04', 55),
(90, 21, 'C129', '<p>Looks great overall!</p>', 3, '2021-03-04 00:52:08', 55),
(91, 16, 'C263', '<p>Is the last one a best practice? Maybe put it under tips</p>', 0, '2021-03-04 01:21:12', 58),
(92, 16, 'P47', '<p>In last paragraph... change to \"An oven may benefit from both adding insulation to the walls and installing...\"</p>', 1, '2021-03-04 01:46:00', 58),
(93, 16, 'C265', '<p><s>Lists the specific heats of common fluids.</s> and <s>List of densities of common fluid.</s></p><p>I\'d say these are evident enough from the titles.</p><p>Also remove \"Heat Exchanger Heat Transfer Coefficients Confirmed valid Dec 16, 2020, 5:33 PM\" from the last link. </p><p></p>', 1, '2021-03-04 01:50:07', 58),
(94, 16, '0', '<p>ʕᵔᴥᵔʔ</p>', 3, '2021-03-04 02:02:02', 58),
(95, 16, '0', '<p>Thanks Ryan. </p><p></p><p>I\'ve made the changes and updated the \"Useful Resources\" card title to one of the preset options in the card titles</p>', 0, '2021-03-07 23:19:11', 57),
(96, 21, '0', '<p>Thanks Julian. The edits have been made and I will look into adding something more in-depth about condensing vs. non-condensing.</p>', 0, '2021-03-07 23:22:30', 57),
(97, 16, 'P47', '<p>I condensed some of the sentences, adjusted some wording and added bold formatting to key words. </p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:14:59', 51),
(98, 16, 'C262', '<p>I added a CON: Heat exchangers may become fouled in some applications, requiring maintenance costs for cleaning.</p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:18:07', 51),
(99, 16, 'C263', '<p>I can see it either way for the last tip per Ryan\'s comments. At first it seemed like an auditor tip, but it would also be a maintenance BP. We should only put it in one place though. I made the tips card Internal - at least for now.</p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:22:35', 51),
(100, 16, 'C265', '<p>Nice resources to reference !</p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:24:59', 51),
(101, 16, '0', '<p>Great new page to make public. Nice work on this part. </p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:25:34', 51),
(102, 21, 'C129', '<p>I pushed the descriptions above the flags</p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:31:10', 51),
(103, 21, '0', '<p>And fiddled with bullet selection and inline items a little.  Nice section overall!</p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:44:30', 51),
(104, 15, 'C95', '<p>Good addition regarding inferring capacity</p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:56:23', 51),
(105, 15, 'C105', '<p>Probably more to add on steam traps as suggested, but we have generally not spent a lot of time on them so I can not think of what. - Fine as is for now.</p>', 0, '2021-03-18 23:58:09', 51),
(106, 15, '0', '<p>Nice work - I am pushing this to publication. </p>', 2, '2021-03-19 00:00:43', 51),
(107, 15, '0', '<p>Pushing to black to publish</p>', 3, '2021-03-19 00:01:07', 51),
(108, 20, '0', '<p>Pushing this to publication</p>', 2, '2021-03-19 00:20:32', 51),
(109, 20, '0', '<p>Pushing this to publication</p>', 3, '2021-03-19 00:20:38', 51),
(110, 25, 'C131', '<p>consider changing \"outside conditions are ideal\" to \"outside conditions are favorable\"</p>', 0, '2021-03-31 19:11:40', 55),
(111, 25, 'C131', '<p>In the 3rd paragraph, I think you can remove \"be used to\" from the first sentence.</p>', 0, '2021-03-31 19:13:03', 55),
(112, 25, 'C131', '<p>Is the cooling medium the same as circulation medium or are you referencing two different things in this section? Maybe call it all cooling or circulation if the same. Could also add some more properties like density etc.</p>', 0, '2021-03-31 19:17:22', 55),
(113, 25, 'C131', '<p>Having additional information on the concept of \"free cooling\" would make a good addition to the page long term</p>', 0, '2021-03-31 19:18:30', 55),
(114, 25, 'C131', '<p>In the VFD opportunity, might be worth discussing that they are particularly suited for varying flows/loads</p>', 0, '2021-03-31 19:20:03', 55),
(115, 25, 'C131', '<p>Consider rewording: </p><p>\"Cooling tower models based off manufacturer data show that reducing fan speeds between 100% and 60% capacity has little impact on cooling tower performance, with larger performance degradation beginning below 50%\"</p><p></p><p>Maybe say \"to 60% capacity\" I think the 100% could confuse people</p>', 0, '2021-03-31 19:22:44', 55),
(116, 25, '0', '<p>Looks good overall!</p>', 0, '2021-03-31 19:23:11', 55),
(117, 25, '0', '<p>Ready for black review.</p>', 2, '2021-03-31 19:23:33', 55),
(118, 25, '0', '<p>I agree with all of Julian\'s comments.</p><p></p><p><strong>A few suggestions, since we\'re thinking the checklist will mostly be a training/assessment tool for newer analysts:</strong></p><p>1) Explain the differences between an open (water) and closed (water/glycol) loop system, and a wet vs dry system. </p><p>2) Likewise explain forced-draft vs induced vs natural and when it might matter</p><p></p><p><strong>Install VFD suggestions</strong></p><p>1) Link to FCAT</p><p>2) \"Energy savings are only realized for fans running at 100% capacity when paired with a reduction in load due to VFDs consuming more power than motors without drives at 100% fan speed.\" can be simplified to \"Energy savings are only realized for fans running at partial loads\"</p><p></p><p><strong>Reduce Fan Speed</strong></p><p>1) I don\'t see how this rule of thumb directly applies, but the cubic law would apply here</p><p>2) Maybe reword the tip so that the implication (don\'t reduce fan speed below 50-60%, or minimum effective partial load is 60%, etc) is forefront. It\'s already fairly clear, but I\'m kind of left wondering when one would choose to operate at say 80% vs 70% if the impact on performance is small either way and the energy savings would be much greater at 70%. </p>', 0, '2021-04-05 18:37:16', 58),
(119, 25, '0', '<p>Nice work! If you choose to add more of the background info suggested then I can take another look at it before submitting to Joe or Ethan for final review.</p>', 3, '2021-04-05 18:40:05', 58),
(120, 25, '0', '<p>Also thinking it might be good to have a separate cooling tower page at this point if enough tech background is added, let\'s bring it up at the next checklist meeting</p>', 0, '2021-04-05 18:41:17', 58),
(121, 6, '0', '<p>I am still a bit unsure of the best way organize the utility information by pages - perhaps [General], [Electrical], [Gas], [Water &amp; Sewer], [Solid Waste], ( But what about [Propane], [Diesel], [Hog Fuel] - all in a Misc Other Category?) - Then We would move Power Factor to the [Electrical] page, and put opportunities specific to each utility on its page (and general opportunities - like pay bills on time - on the general page] </p>', 0, '2021-05-25 23:02:04', 51),
(122, 30, 'C27', '<p>consider changing \"uncorrected\" to undetected in the Reduce Compressed Air Leaks opportunity</p>', 0, '2021-05-26 20:06:54', 55),
(123, 30, 'C27', '<p>The standard data to collect link is a good idea</p>', 0, '2021-05-26 20:08:13', 55),
(124, 30, 'C27', '<p>the Analysis Template link took me to a blank page</p>', 0, '2021-05-26 20:09:33', 55),
(125, 30, 'C27', '<p>A general note: opportunity headers are capitalized on some of the pages on the walkthrough. we may want to discuss a standard for formatting these</p>', 0, '2021-05-26 20:12:24', 55),
(126, 25, '0', '<p>I rewrote \"Installation of a cooling tower reduce condensor water temperatures which reduces the work required by a compressor.\" to say \"Industrial refrigeration commonly uses a cooling tower at the condenser, to bring refrigerant to a lower condensing temperature/pressure, reducing the work required by the refrigeration compressor. \"</p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:15:03', 51),
(127, 25, '0', '<p>I changed the sub-bullet icons for \"Cooling medium properties\" to dots instead of pencils, split one item into two, and put them in line.</p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:16:28', 51),
(128, 30, 'C27', '<p>consider changing \"significant unneeded\" to \"unnecessary\" in the Interlock opportunity description. Also the second sentence is a little confusing so maybe reword it.</p>', 0, '2021-05-26 20:18:19', 55),
(129, 25, '0', '<p>I moved the \"How a cooling tower functions\" graphic above all of the opportunities</p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:18:42', 51),
(130, 30, '0', '<p>Overall looks good! Lots of solid information. </p>', 2, '2021-05-26 20:18:53', 55),
(131, 25, '0', '<p>I added \" (to evaluate chiller load) \" to \"Power quality analyzer\"</p><p></p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:20:55', 51),
(132, 25, '0', '<p>Seems like since the following is in the top intro, it should not be in the details of \"Reduce cooling tower fan speed\"</p><p></p><p> \"Cooling towers may be used as standalone equipment or added to a chiller system to reduce the load when outside conditions are ideal. There are three common types of cooling towers used today: forced-draft, induced-draft, and hyperbolic (natural draft)\" </p><p></p><p>I made it internal in the second case but should likely go. </p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:34:32', 51),
(133, 25, '0', '<p>I changed \"based off\" to \"based on\". The former is becoming common in casual speech (to my consternation!:-) but the latter is correct grammatically. </p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:38:53', 51),
(134, 25, '0', '<p>I added \"as low as \" to \"speeds to 60% capacity\" for \"speeds to as low as  60% capacity\"</p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:41:17', 51),
(135, 25, '0', '<p>I am a little confused about one data item you list under \"<strong>Utilize cooling towers to bypass chillers in cooler weather</strong>\".  \"<em>Approach temperature logged for a year or cooling tower inlet temperature logged for a year</em>.</p><p></p><p>Approach temperature would typically not change a lot but we do want them to evaluate approach on the assessment day by comparing the wet bulb temperature at the time to the temperature of water exiting the cooling tower.  Not sure why you roll it with <em>i\"nlet temperature logged for a year</em>.\" (Suggesting logging anything for a year is problematic for an assessment. ) </p><p></p><p>I broke them apart and edited approach. </p>', 1, '2021-05-26 20:51:49', 51),
(136, 25, '0', '<p>I changed<em>: \"Ambient wet bulb logged for a year, or period of interest\" to \"</em>Ambient wet bulb over the year, or period of interest. Data can often be obtained on-line\"</p>', 1, '2021-05-26 21:42:10', 51),
(137, 25, '0', '<p>I changed \"Chiller energy usage logged  for a year\" to \"Chiller energy usage logged <u>or estimated</u> for a year</p>', 1, '2021-05-26 21:45:14', 51),
(138, 25, '0', '<p>I added a fan law rule of thumb per Ryan\'s suggestion : </p><p></p><p>Required fan power varies with the cube of the speed. For instance: if the fan is dropped to 50% speed, the power will drop to 12.5% of full load power (0.5 x 0.5 x 0.5 = 0.125)</p>', 1, '2021-05-26 21:51:18', 51),
(140, 25, '0', '<p>I added \"Sling psychrometer\" as equipment to use when considering <strong>Utilize cooling towers to bypass chillers in cooler weather</strong></p>', 1, '2021-05-26 21:57:31', 51),
(141, 33, '0', '<p>Good work!</p>', 2, '2021-05-26 22:11:26', 58),
(143, 28, '0', '<p>The changes look good. The only thing I noticed was that \"Standard Data\" under the \"Data to Collect\" did not appear to be linked to anything. I am not sure if this was intentional or not.</p>', 2, '2021-05-27 22:13:44', 79),
(144, 31, 'C77', '<p>Is there a reason that Reduce Inlet Air Temperature is for internal access? if so, the Data to collect should also be internal.</p>', 1, '2021-05-27 23:46:33', 61),
(145, 31, 'C77', '<p>While a link to the standard data to collect is a good idea, it doesn\'t appear that the other technologies have this. I suggest removing</p>', 1, '2021-05-27 23:55:35', 61),
(146, 31, 'C77', '<p>Change the rule of thumb to: \"Improves efficiency by 1.9% (scfm/kW) per 10 F reduction at inlet\"</p><p></p><p>I think it can be assumed that the reader will understand this only applies around standard operating conditions. If you do not agree then this might need to be an additional caveat  </p>', 1, '2021-05-28 00:01:52', 61),
(147, 31, 'C77', '<p>It might be a good idea to include something stating why short cycling is a problem or how much energy is wasted by short cycling</p>', 1, '2021-05-28 00:32:08', 61),
(148, 31, 'C77', '<p>Analyst templet should be internal resource</p>', 1, '2021-05-28 00:40:51', 61),
(149, 31, '0', '<p>I know that it has been suggested that there be a page for VFDs. It might be a good idea to put an place holder for a link. This link would need to be internal since it is only a placeholder</p>', 0, '2021-05-28 00:43:43', 61),
(151, 31, '0', '<p>Really like the description for the using a sequence! It is very clear and concise, and allows non technical people to understand. Nice!</p>', 2, '2021-05-28 00:47:26', 61),
(152, 28, '0', '<p>The \"Standard Data\" link works on the actual compressed air page but isn\'t working on the review page. Good catch but it seems to be working fine. </p>', 0, '2021-06-07 16:58:31', 60),
(153, 34, '0', '<p>General Comment</p>', 0, '2021-07-28 18:31:41', 61),
(154, 34, 'C329', '<p>Add content</p>', 0, '2021-07-28 18:32:08', 61),
(155, 34, '0', '<p>Looks good done</p>', 2, '2021-07-28 18:33:22', 61);
